Migrations.

Create the first revision against a running database:

    alembic revision --autogenerate -m "initial schema"
    alembic upgrade head

Autogenerate compares app/models.py against the database, so a model that is
not imported there is invisible to it -- and alembic will propose to DROP its
table. Add every new model to app/models.py before generating.

app/database/db.py still calls create_all() on startup, which is convenient
for a first run but only ever CREATEs -- it never ALTERs. Once migrations are
the source of truth, drop that call from the lifespan in app/main.py.

Generate it against POSTGRES, not SQLite. Autogenerating against SQLite bakes
in that dialect's defaults -- server_default=text('(CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)') where
Postgres wants now() -- and those defaults end up in the real schema.
